1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,200
Gauss conjectured this, in
a slightly different form,

2
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:09,250
and Hadamard and de la
Vallée Poussin proved it.

3
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:12,400
It is called the Prime Number Theorem,

4
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:14,950
and it is the subject of this video.

5
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:19,500
Before the full proof, Chebyshev
proved a weaker version,

6
00:00:19,650 --> 00:00:22,250
bounding the ratio from above and below

7
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,400
but the limit is not found,

8
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:27,550
and it fails for percentages
that are too small.

9
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:32,300
Later, Riemann developed a revolutionary
strategy for such problems.

10
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:39,150
It was this strategy that eventually
led to the solution of the problem

11
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,700
and to much fascinating mathematics.

